= Introduction

Establishing Downlink. . .

Welcome to Telemetry Troubles!

You begin your career with one of the Outer Rim League companies. There are many ways you can apply your talent within the League, but the fact that you are holding this playbook right now suggests you are considering a path in spacecraft systems engineering.

Congratulations! A perfect choice! You are looking at life full of debugging all-nighters, coffee overconsumption, and HARD deadlines. And by HARD, we mean like really hard, set in stone, uncompromised, unnegotiable deadlines - planets and moons, after all, don't wait for you in orbit, and encounter timelines are pretty much fixed at the moment of your probe launch.

So relax and enjoy your ride. Debugging deep-space probes might seem like a daunting task, but it is totally achievable with some patience, focus, and persistence. It is not rocket science after all\.\.\. Well, it kind of is, but not the hardest part of it.

And this is only the beginning of your troubles!

The following chapters cover the full depth of our deep-space exploration program and associated challenges. We start with a QuickStart Guide, followed by the description of DUSTY-12 features and full technical specifications.

The second part of this book contains hints for upcoming experiments.

After the technical section and hints, you can find background information on various aspects of Telemetry Troubles, including the current outer rim business climate and a glossary of the most commonly used technical terms.

Are you ready to lead humanity into outer space?




